{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>If brothers dwell together.</b> They [the Karaites] also said that they are not actual brothers but only relatives, and they brought proof from Boaz — but they said nothing, for there is no mention of levirate marriage there, only redemption. And what is the reason to mention \"together\"? If they were in one city or in one courtyard, or if they loved one another. And they said that the verse says ויבמה, and this is a sign that she is not a yevamah in [the technical] sense, but [the word functions] only as a name, like שבה יבמתך. But they have acted foolishly and ignorantly, for it is explicitly stated regarding the sons of Judah, ויבם אותה, and he is her yavam; likewise יבמתך, because they belong to two brothers. And every man of understanding knows that the commandments given to Moses — which are negative commandments — were not forbidden before then; and had a person refrained from them before Moses preceded, the matter would not have been evil in the eyes of HaShem — even though He wrote, \"for all these abominations the men of the land who are before you have done,\" and we do not find a prophet who warned them. Now the verse states concerning Onan that he did not give seed to his brother, and it was evil in the eyes of YHWH. Therefore we will rely on the tradition that they are actual brothers." "<b>And he has no son.</b> For if he has a son, there is no need, for she is forbidden." "And the meaning of <b>together.</b> As the words of the translators [Onkelos]." "<b>To a foreign man.</b> Meaning an outsider, if the yavam so wishes."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The antecedents of 'they' are inferred as the Karaites from the polemical context; the Hebrew says only 'they.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:48.282952785Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}